"answer": "Project Zenith is an AI-driven initiative launched in 2029 aimed at developing advanced mental health support systems, including chatbots and virtual therapists, with a goal to reach 5 million users by 2035. The project has received executive budget approval of $2 million, though specific allocations have been adjusted, including a $550,000 general budget and a $55,000 compliance plan budget. The team is expanding with new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, with an onboarding session scheduled for September 10th. The project is moving from the design phase to the development phase, led by Omar Jensen. R&D is currently gathering ideas for enhancing data visualization tools, with proposals due by July 20th. Security protocols are being updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective next January. Additionally, the company is exploring partnership opportunities with TechInnovate to leverage their AI technology."
